# Claude Code settings stay LOCAL. None of `.claude/` is tracked.
#
# `.claude/settings.json` used to be committed, carrying
#
#     "enabledPlugins": {
#       "modern-code-guidelines@modern-code-guidelines": true,
#       "frontend-design@claude-plugins-official": true
#     }
#
# which enabled code from two marketplaces that the file itself never declared,
# at no pinned version, for everyone who cloned this repository. That is a
# dependency with none of the properties this repo demands of a dependency: it
# is not named to a source, not pinned to a revision, and not visible in any
# diff when it changes.
#
# THE DECISION WAS MADE TWICE. It was first removed on the branch that hardened
# the workflows, for the reason above. I put it back during integration, judging
# that a personal site with one contributor is not the case that reasoning is
# about, and that changing the owner's own tooling was not part of the task. The
# owner then asked for it out of version control, which settles it and says the
# original change was right: the file is a per-developer preference, and a
# preference that arrives by clone is not a preference.
#
# Untracked rather than deleted, so it keeps working locally for whoever has it.
# Want the plugins? Enable them for yourself:
#     /plugin  (in Claude Code)  — writes under .claude/
.claude/
